   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are CLEAN (DRC 0, LVS match at every point).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe original `/nand2.icl` had three compounding problems:\n1. **Gate pitch too small** \u2014 gates were spaced with only a 0.20 \u00b5m gap (needs \u22650.21 \u00b5m poly-poly, and \u22650.54 \u00b5m centre-to-centre for gate-contact pads).\n2. **Drain contact too close to gate** \u2014 the p-row Y contact `c4` sat between the two gates and overlapped/violated the licon.11 rule against gate B.\n3. **Gate contacts too close together** \u2014 both gate contacts were centred on their gates with no outward shift, causing poly.2/mcon.2/met1.2 violations between the contact pads and their met1 port enclosures.\n\nI rewrote the geometry following the verified `l1_param_nand2.icl` pattern: a single shared diffusion island per row (`dw = 2*L + 0.81`), gates placed at the ends (`left=(nd.left+0.265)`, `right=(nd.right-0.265)`), drain/source contact columns via `array licon ... left_of/right_of/between`, gate contacts pushed outwards (`cx=(ga.cx-0.1)`, `cx=(gb.cx+0.1)`) so the pads clear, `cb` computed only from n-row items (per lesson 1), and `route Y layers=m1` to join the misaligned n/p Y drains (per lesson 6). `width=6` columns (2.76 \u00b5m) fits the diffusion at L=0.25. Nominal + all 5 sweep points pass DRC/LVS.",
