   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are CLEAN \u2014 DRC 0 and LVS match at every point.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe original `/nand3.icl` had one broken edit: it used `strap li from=c1l to=c6l net=Y` to join the output between the n-row and p-row drains, which don't line up vertically (lesson 12). This caused a compile error (\"strap: the two objects do not line up\").\n\n**Fixes applied:**\n1. Replaced the misaligned `strap` with `route Y layers=m1,m2` (lesson 6/12) \u2014 routes join nets that don't line up.\n2. Added intermediate node contacts `cn2` (net=n2 between gates A-B) and `cn1` (net=n1 between gates B-C) on the n-side diffusion, with `route n1` and `route n2` so LVS can see the series nodes (lesson 5).\n3. Included those contact strips in the `cb = max(...)` calculation (lesson 1 \u2014 cb only uses n-row items).\n4. Fixed `nd1` end margin from `g1.left - 0.18` to `g1.left - 0.265` to satisfy `poly.7` (diffusion must extend 0.25 beyond each gate).\n5. Kept a single continuous p-diffusion island (avoiding the poly.7/nwell errors from splitting it into 3 small islands).\n\nThe cell is parametric: every dimension derives from `L`, `WN`, `WP`, `H` via `max(0.28, 0.54 - L)` gate spacing and `0.265` end margins, so it passes all sweep points including L=0.25 and width x1.9.",
