   "final_message": "The cell is now clean across all 6 sweep points.\n\n**Problem:** The existing `/a21oi.icl` had an LVS mismatch \u2014 net `n2` was in two separate pieces (`c4l` and `c6l`, both on the p-diffusion `pd1`) that were never joined. Per lesson 5, an internal net running from drain to gate inside the cell needs its drain li strips and gate contact li labelled with the same net and a `route` to connect them.\n\n**Fix:** Added `route n2 layers=m1,m2` before the Y route, joining the two n2 pieces into one connected net. Everything else (device lines, gate order, contact placement, well, ports) was left unchanged.\n\n**Result:** DRC 0 errors, LVS match at nominal and all 5 sweep points (L=0.18/0.25, widths x0.85/x1.35/x1.9, H up to 4.08).",
