   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean. The repair is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe cell `/and2.icl` was broken by one edit that introduced `pd1.bottom - 0.05` into the `cb = max(...)` calculation for gate-contact height. Per lesson 1, `cb` may use **only n-row items** \u2014 including the p-row (`pd1.bottom`) pushed every gate contact up into the p-tap row, causing 131 DRC errors (licon.14, li.3, li.c2, licon.9, poly.2) and an LVS short of inputs to VPWR.\n\n**Fixes applied:**\n1. **Removed `pd1.bottom - 0.05` from `cb`** \u2014 now `cb = max(nd1.top + 0.19, nd2.top + 0.19, c1l.top + 0.25, c2l.top + 0.25, c3l.top + 0.25, c4l.top + 0.25)` (n-row only).\n2. **Added output routing** \u2014 n-side drain `c1l` and p-side drain `c5l` (both net=X) don't line up, so both get mcon contacts and `route X layers=m1,m2` joins them; `port X out on=xp` puts the pin on routed met1.\n3. **Added `route n1 layers=m1,m2`** to connect the internal net n1 (drain li strips + gate contact li share net=n1).\n\nResult: DRC 0, LVS match at nominal, and all 6 sweep points clean (L=0.18/0.25, widths \u00d70.85/\u00d71.35/\u00d71.9, H up to 4.08).",
