   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean. The repair is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe original `/or2.icl` had two fundamental problems:\n\n1. **Gate pitch too small**: Gates A and B were spaced with only 0.2 \u00b5m gap (centre-to-centre 0.35 \u00b5m for L=0.15), violating the 0.54 \u00b5m minimum pitch needed for gate contacts. This caused cascading poly.2, licon.11, met1.2, and mcon.2 errors.\n\n2. **Diffusion boundaries used gate centres instead of edges**: The diffusion `xspan` was computed from gate centre positions rather than gate edges, so the diffusion didn't extend 0.265 \u00b5m beyond each gate edge, causing poly.7 and licon.1 errors.\n\n**Fix applied**: Rewrote the geometry section to compute gate centre positions with proper pitch (`max(0.28, 0.54 - L)` between adjacent gates, `max(0.80, 0.54 - L)` for the island break between B and n2), then derived gate edges from centres, and set diffusion boundaries from gate edges \u00b1 0.265 \u00b5m. Gate contacts use only n-row items in the `cb` max (per lesson 1), and the internal net n2 and output X are connected via `route` statements. Cell width increased to 8 columns (0.46 \u00b5m each) to fit at L=0.25.",
